#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
apply-nodalis-v4-fixes.py

Applies the v4 changes to your Nodalis index.html in place.

    python3 apply-nodalis-v4-fixes.py index.html

What it does
    * unique note titles, Windows-style: "Meeting", "Meeting (1)", "Meeting (2)"
      with a live warning as you type and a command to fix existing duplicates
    * no keyboard shortcut can belong to two commands, ever; the two that
      already clashed in your build are fixed
    * Trash: deleted notes are kept for 30 days and can be restored
    * Templates: any note in your Templates folder, with {{date}}-style fields
    * the command palette learns what you use and puts it first
    * an aliases editor, so [[other names]] for a note are two clicks away
    * "Check my vault" - one report for duplicates, shortcut clashes, dead
      links, empty notes, stale reminders and where your work is being saved

It refuses to run rather than half-apply:
    * every edit is matched exactly once, or nothing is written
    * a .bak copy is made first
    * running it twice is detected and stops with a message

No dependencies. Python 3.6+.
"""
import io
import os
import shutil
import sys

